    <string name="screensaver_title">Automatic StandBy on the lock screen</string>
    <string name="screensaver_body">Android lets apps appear on a locked phone automatically only through the system screen saver. Choose “StandBy Clock” as the screen saver and set it to start while charging. When the screen times out on the charger, StandBy appears over the lock screen; in landscape you get the full display, otherwise it turns the screen off after 30 seconds.</string>
    <string name="lockscreen_title">Lock screen and security</string>
    <string name="lockscreen_body">StandBy can be shown on top of the lock screen but never unlocks your phone or replaces your secure lock screen. Notifications and apps stay protected. Exiting StandBy while locked returns you to your normal lock screen.</string>
    <string name="device_tips_title">Tips for your phone</string>
    <string name="tip_samsung">Samsung: the screen saver is under Settings › Display › Screen saver (some One UI versions hide it; search Settings for “Screen saver”). Disable “Put app to sleep” for StandBy Clock in Battery settings if StandBy closes unexpectedly.</string>
    <string name="tip_oneplus">OnePlus: Settings › Display may not list a screen saver on every OxygenOS build. Use Start StandBy, then lock the phone. Allow StandBy Clock under Battery › Battery optimisation if it is closed in the background.</string>
    <string name="tip_xiaomi">Xiaomi / Redmi / POCO: HyperOS and MIUI usually remove the system screen saver. Use Start StandBy, then lock the phone. Set Battery saver to “No restrictions” for StandBy Clock and enable “Show on Lock screen” in the app\'s Other permissions.</string>
    <string name="tip_oppo">OPPO / realme: ColorOS may hide the screen saver. Use Start StandBy, then lock. Allow “Show on lock screen” / floating windows for StandBy Clock if the lock screen hides it.</string>
    <string name="tip_vivo">vivo / iQOO: Funtouch / OriginOS may hide the screen saver. Use Start StandBy, then lock. Allow “Lock screen display” for StandBy Clock in app permissions if needed.</string>
    <string name="tip_pixel">Pixel: Settings › Display › Screen saver › StandBy Clock, then “When to start” › While charging. Pixel tablets also offer Hub mode, which is a separate system feature.</string>
    <string name="tip_motorola">Motorola: Settings › Display › Screen saver (if present) supports StandBy Clock. Otherwise use Start StandBy and lock the phone.</string>
    <string name="tip_generic">If your phone has Settings › Display › Screen saver, choose StandBy Clock there for fully automatic StandBy. Otherwise use Start StandBy and then lock the phone.</string>

